## SQ-JFP-01 | pump water from a Create tank into a Supplementaries jar (both pump directions tried)
@group A
@commands Place `supplementaries:jar`; `/setblock` a `create:fluid_tank` beside it with `/data merge block` 4000 mB water (or a creative fluid tank), mechanical pump + pipe from the tank to the jar, creative motor 64 RPM; wait 20 s; `/data get block <jar>`
@pass `FluidHolder` water, count 12; no `Error occurred` in latest.log
@fails No capability: `JarFluidPipes.register` not reached (Supplementaries check) or the attach event filter
@from batches/r1102b/s5_R_A.qb
# layout at x+400 (forceloaded): tank T, pump P (small cog, axis x), jar J along +x; cogwheel above P, creative motor
# above T facing east drives it at 64 RPM (ScrollValue 64; Speed read back). Create's flow direction depends on facing and rotation sign, so each phase is run
# with the pump facing east and then west; one of them fills the jar (JFP-01), the next drains it back (JFP-02).
> fill {S5H1+399} {S5H2} {S5H3-1} {S5H1+403} {S5H2+2} {S5H3+1} minecraft:air
> setblock {S5H1+400} {S5H2} {S5H3} create:fluid_tank
sleep 2
> data merge block {S5H1+400} {S5H2} {S5H3} {TankContent:{FluidName:"minecraft:water",Amount:4000}}
> setblock {S5H1+402} {S5H2} {S5H3} supplementaries:jar
> setblock {S5H1+401} {S5H2} {S5H3} create:mechanical_pump[facing=east]
> setblock {S5H1+401} {S5H2+1} {S5H3} create:cogwheel[axis=x]
> setblock {S5H1+400} {S5H2+1} {S5H3} create:creative_motor[facing=east]{ScrollValue:64}
> setblock {S5H1+401} {S5H2} {S5H3} create:mechanical_pump[facing=east]
sleep 2
> data get block {S5H1+400} {S5H2+1} {S5H3} Speed
> data get block {S5H1+401} {S5H2} {S5H3} Speed
sleep 58
> say JFP phase 1 pump east
> data get block {S5H1+402} {S5H2} {S5H3}
> data get block {S5H1+400} {S5H2} {S5H3} TankContent
count has the following block data: -?64\.0f$ >= 2
expect has the following block data: .*FluidHolder
reject (Unknown (item|block|block type|entity)|does not (have|accept)|Incorrect argument for command|Unknown or incomplete command|That position is not loaded|No player was found|no such bot|no such item|Invalid (block state|tag)|\[(zq|s5)\] (error|no player))
look phase 1 or phase 2 (next row) ends with the jar FluidHolder water, count 12, and the tank down to 1000 mB; no Error occurred line

## SQ-JFP-02 | reverse the pump: the jar drains back into the tank
@group same
@commands Reverse the pump; empty tank on the far side
@pass Tank 3000 mB water, jar `FluidHolder` empty, `ForgeCaps` has no PendingMb
@fails Drain returns the wrong fluid: `contents()` / `getForgeFluid`
@from batches/r1102b/s5_R_A.qb
> setblock {S5H1+401} {S5H2} {S5H3} create:mechanical_pump[facing=west]
sleep 60
> say JFP phase 2 pump west
> data get block {S5H1+402} {S5H2} {S5H3}
> data get block {S5H1+400} {S5H2} {S5H3} TankContent
> setblock {S5H1+401} {S5H2} {S5H3} create:mechanical_pump[facing=east]
sleep 60
> say JFP phase 3 pump east
> data get block {S5H1+402} {S5H2} {S5H3}
> data get block {S5H1+400} {S5H2} {S5H3} TankContent
shell ! grep -n 'Error occurred' logs/latest.log | grep -iE 'jar|fluid|supplementaries'
look across phases 1-3: one direction fills the jar to water 12 from the tank, the other empties the jar and the tank gets the water back (row: tank 3000 mB from an empty far-side tank; here the same tank holds 4000 again); after a drain the jar FluidHolder is empty and ForgeCaps has no PendingMb

